{"meta":{"format_version":"4.10","model_format":"free","box_uv":false},"name":"carcass","model_identifier":"carcass","visible_box":[1,1,0],"variable_placeholders":"","variable_placeholder_buttons":[],"timeline_setups":[],"unhandled_root_fields":{"description":"# carcass\n\nGeneric animal carcass\n\n- Left where an animal falls (milestone 4's carcass prop) for every animal without its own carcass: the bear, deer, hare and wolf have `carcass_bear`, `carcass_deer`, `carcass_hare` and `carcass_wolf`.\n- A mid-sized hoofed body lying on its right side, legs out stiff, eye closed, a small pool of blood. Brown hide, pale belly, flat colours.\n- About 1 m nose to tail (1 unit = 2.8125 cm); scale it per species (the client's drawn carcass uses 0.35 for small animals and 1.6 for the largest).\n- Head to -Z, lying on y = 0, centred on the origin. No clips: a static prop.\n- 28 cubes, texture 64 x 128.\n- When its meat is gone, swap in `carcass_bones`.\n"},"resolution":{"width":64,"height":128},"elements":[{"name":"barrel","box_uv":false,"rescale":false,"locked":false,"light_emission":0,"render_order":"default","allow_mirror_modeling":true,"from":[-15.0,0.0,-9.0],"to":[-2.0,11.0,23.0],"autouv":0,"color":0,"inflate":0.0,"origin":[-8.0,0.0,7.0],"faces":{"north":{"uv":[0,32,13.0,43.0],"texture":0},"south":{"uv":[0,32,13.0,43.0],"texture":0},"east":{"uv":[28,0,60.0,11.0],"texture":0},"west":{"uv":[28,0,60.0,11.0],"texture":0},"up":{"uv":[0,0,13.0,32.0],"texture":0},"down":{"uv":[0,0,13.0,32.0],"texture":0}},"type":"cube","uuid":"c9364ba0-41ae-50be-830e-d722247db5d3"},{"name":"back","box_uv":false,"rescale":false,"locked":false,"light_emission":0,"render_order":"default","allow_mirror_modeling":true,"from":[-16.0,1.0,-8.0],"to":[-15.0,10.0,21.0],"autouv":0,"color":0,"inflate":0.0,"origin":[-8.0,0.0,7.0],"faces":{"north":{"uv":[55,43,56.0,52.0],"texture":0},"south":{"uv":[55,43,56.0,52.0],"texture":0},"east":{"uv":[27,32,56.0,41.0],"texture":0},"west":{"uv":[27,32,56.0,41.0],"texture