":"bd0590db-3add-53f9-bf50-0fb19eafd978","export":true,"mirror_uv":false,"isOpen":false,"locked":false,"visibility":true,"autouv":0,"rotation":[0.0,0.0,0.0],"children":["976fb213-ac45-59f5-bbbf-5d0cdaf6b61d","e3dd4e8e-2e82-571d-a2bb-faeab38d837b","a2b002d8-b442-54b9-9969-c2921369534e","d038f21b-2642-50a9-9615-d0ed9b265bbd","6f9d5cb4-35bd-5cf6-863c-836bfddf7f42","d92da07d-d927-58c9-b835-545d036ea9c2","05dba0a8-45ba-55b7-ad78-940fa56cd8dd","d6694efd-58f5-54d4-b411-c22f934ef32a"]},{"name":"legs","origin":[-2.0,0.0,7.0],"color":0,"uuid":"d38f1c94-4539-5703-ab02-4605ddaa834a","export":true,"mirror_uv":false,"isOpen":false,"locked":false,"visibility":true,"autouv":0,"rotation":[0.0,0.0,0.0],"children":["59ebe494-c978-5dec-9fb8-f23abd742ef8","43cadaa8-7702-57ac-bdfd-81945afa053d","c2c9088a-c276-5316-9648-00af9b2c8315","a9ac0887-632c-5144-bd66-e9d5335fac95","aae25519-ac05-5bb2-9090-a37db6e1f061","23894a80-f1cb-534d-9922-7be806457f06","9dbf6730-afce-5a2d-a0a5-054ae4c1d8c8","a12443e9-566c-5f17-9c6b-d46d2d8f725a","b2915a7a-b96f-5320-943d-6114c24290ba","3f4f9891-6e56-5c6c-ac63-11baa749818f","eccbd4b0-2f36-5065-a943-728761776f52","bf8827c3-4248-5ab3-97f1-634099e8f421"]}]}]}],"textures":[{"path":"carcass.png","name":"carcass.png","folder":"","namespace":"","id":"0","width":64,"height":128,"uv_width":64,"uv_height":128,"particle":false,"use_as_default":true,"layers_enabled":false,"sync_to_project":"","render_mode":"default","render_sides":"auto","frame_time":1,"frame_order_type":"loop","frame_order":"","frame_interpolate":false,"visible":true,"internal":true,"saved":true,"uuid":"97d23e24-4714-576e-ab66-7e5cb1ddedef","relative_path":"carcass.png","source":"data:image/png;base64,"}],"animations":[],"description":"# carcass\n\nGeneric animal carcass\n\n- Left where an animal falls (milestone 4's carcass prop) for every animal without its own carcass: the bear, deer, hare and wolf have `carcass_bear`, `carcass_deer`, `carcass_hare` and `carcass_wolf`.\n- A mid-sized hoofed body lying on its right side, legs out stiff, eye closed, a small pool of blood. Brown hide, pale belly, flat colours.\n- About 1 m nose to tail (1 unit = 2.8125 cm); scale it per species (the client's drawn carcass uses 0.35 for small animals and 1.6 for the largest).\n- Head to -Z, lying on y = 0, centred on the origin. No clips: a static prop.\n- 28 cubes, texture 64 x 128.\n- When its meat is gone, swap in `carcass_bones`.\n"}